    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21">

                <pb facs="0038" n="22" xml:id="pg22"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation (4)/7–1647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-16T17:00:00-04:00">July 16, 1947—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>584. Depcirtels July 3, 9:30 a.m. and July 8, 8 p.m.<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d21-f1"/> Last night Chile sent following reply to Pan American
                    Union on Rio Conference consultation: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Point I. Question 1—affirmative answer.</p>
                        <p>Point I. Question 2—affirmative reply, although possibility might be
                            considered of reaching prior agreements on nature, scope and
                            desirability of immediate help in event of armed attack.</p>
                        <p>Point II. Questions 1 and 2—the two-thirds principle accepted. Govt of
                            Chile considers it advisable distinguish between obligations of American
                            states in accordance with nature of measures adopted (political,
                            financial, military). In any case, it believes there should be agreement
                            on part of signatory states which have not agreed to measures taken not
                            to do anything that might jeopardize their fulfillment.</p>
                        <p>Point III. It is accepted that creation of a military organization should
                            be referred to Bogotá Conference.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
